{
  "title": "Combining Text (String Concatenation)",
  "subtitle": "Joining Strings with the + Operator",
  "topic": "3.2 • STRING CONCATENATION",
  "body": "<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; width: 100%;\">\n  <div style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 4px; width: 100%;\">\n    <div style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px #111111; padding: 4px 14px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: 900; font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px;\">\n      3.2 • Text Manipulation\n    </div>\n    <h1 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 8px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      Combining <hlt>Text</hlt> with +\n    </h1>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #222222; margin: 0 auto; max-width: 640px;\">\n      In Python, the plus operator <code>+</code> does not only add numbers—when placed between strings (text), it glues them together end-to-end! This is called <strong>string concatenation</strong>.\n    </p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"background: #93c5fd; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 20px;\">\n    <span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">\n      The Glue Analogy\n    </span>\n    <h2 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 10px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      Gluing Paper Strips Together\n    </h2>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 12px 0; line-height: 1.5;\">\n      Think of strings as words on paper strips. Using <code>+</code> glues them together. If you want a space between words, you must glue an explicit space string <code>\" \"</code> in between!\n    </p>\n    <div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 #111111; padding: 12px 14px; font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; color: #f0f6fc; font-size: 14px; border-radius: 4px;\">\n      first = <span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"Good\"</span><br/>\n      second = <span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"Morning\"</span><br/><br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># Without space:</span><br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(first + second)          <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># Outputs: \"GoodMorning\"</span><br/><br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># With space:</span><br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(first + <span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\" \"</span> + second)    <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># Outputs: \"Good Morning\"</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"background: #fbcfe8; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 20px;\">\n    <span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">\n      Operator Behavior • Math vs Text\n    </span>\n    <h2 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 10px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      Same Operator (+), Different Data Types\n    </h2>\n    <div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 #111111; padding: 12px 14px; font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; color: #f0f6fc; font-size: 14px; border-radius: 4px;\">\n      <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># 1. Numbers: Mathematical Addition</span><br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(<span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">10</span> + <span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">20</span>)      <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># Outputs: 30</span><br/><br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># 2. Strings: Text Concatenation</span><br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(<span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"10\"</span> + <span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"20\"</span>)  <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># Outputs: \"1020\"</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"background: #fed7aa; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 18px;\">\n    <span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">\n      Type Safety • str() Conversion\n    </span>\n    <h3 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Joining Text and Numbers</h3>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: #111111; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.5;\">\n      You cannot directly add text and an integer: <code>\"Level \" + 5</code> causes a TypeError. To join them, convert the integer to a string using <code>str(5)</code>:\n    </p>\n    <div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 2px solid #111111; padding: 10px; font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; color: #f0f6fc; font-size: 13px; border-radius: 4px;\">\n      level = <span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">5</span><br/>\n      message = <span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"Level: \"</span> + <span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">str</span>(level)<br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(message)  <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># Outputs: \"Level: 5\"</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>"
}